  "meta": {
    "templateCredsSetupCompleted": false,
    "description": "Called from the Main Email Router's Account Status Branch whenever an inbound email (including follow-ups) arrives from a SUSPENDED account. Implements the KYC-equivalent re-verification referenced by FR-6.6 as three ordered, bounded-retry gates: identity challenge (name/DOB/last transaction amount), phone OTP, and a mandatory staff review that alone can lift the suspension. Repeated identity or OTP failure escalates as a possible fraud signal rather than looping indefinitely."
  },
